__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Print artifacts are build output, not source. `printing/generate-all.sh`
# rebuilds every one of them from the markdown, and committing them cost
# a full new copy of each file per rebuild — a PDF is compressed binary,
# so git cannot store one as a small difference from the last one the way
# it does for prose. See printing/README.md.
printing/*.pdf

# The generated HTML, same reasoning as the PDFs and applied later. Fifteen
# files, eight thousand lines, rewritten by ninety-six commits in three
# weeks, and nobody reads them. What they were for was the staleness diff,
# and `printing/manifest.txt` does that in fifteen lines instead — one per
# artifact, with a hash. The HTML is output; the manifest is the record.
printing/*.html
